PROJECT: Attention-based image captioning (Show, Attend and Tell, Xu et al. 2015) in PyTorch.
DATA: MS COCO 2014 images with the Karpathy split (dataset_coco.json). Karpathy restval is merged into train. Captions come pre-tokenised (sentences[].tokens). Vocab = words with frequency >= 5 in train; specials <pad>=0 <start>=1 <end>=2 <unk>=3. Train captions longer than 50 tokens are dropped.
ENCODER: torchvision ResNet-50 with ImageNet weights, avgpool and fc removed -> (B,2048,7,7) -> (B,49,2048). Frozen by default; optional fine-tune of layer3 and layer4 later. Eval/inference transform: Resize((224,224)) + ImageNet normalisation (no crop, so the 7x7 grid covers the whole image). Train transform: Resize(256) + RandomCrop(224) + normalisation.
ATTENTION: additive soft attention. e_i = w^T tanh(W_enc a_i + W_dec h); alpha = softmax over the 49 regions; context = sum_i alpha_i a_i. attention_dim = 512.
DECODER: LSTMCell, embed_dim 512, decoder_dim 512, dropout 0.5. h0 and c0 come from Linear(mean of encoder features). A sigmoid gate beta = sigmoid(Linear(h)) scales the context. Input at step t = concat(embedding(previous word), beta * context). Output = Linear(dropout(h)) -> vocab logits. Teacher forcing in training. Variable length captions: sort the batch by length (descending) and at step t only run the first batch_size_t rows.
LOSS: cross-entropy over non-padded positions + 1.0 * mean((1 - sum_t alpha_t)^2) (doubly stochastic attention regularisation).
OPTIM: Adam, lr 4e-4 for the decoder, gradient clipping 5.0, torch.autocast (AMP) on GPU.
DECODING: DecodingStrategy interface with Greedy and BeamSearch (k = 3 or 5). Max length 50.
INFERENCE OUTPUT: caption (str), words (list of str), attention (num_words x 7 x 7 floats), time_ms.
METRICS: BLEU-4, METEOR, CIDEr from pycocoevalcap on the Karpathy test split. NLTK has no CIDEr.
CHECKPOINT CONTRACT (.pt): model_state, vocab (word -> id), config {encoder_dim 2048, attention_dim, embed_dim, decoder_dim, dropout, max_len, num_regions 49}, epoch, val_bleu4. Always save vocab.json next to the .pt.
REPO: ml/captioning/{data,vocab,encoder,attention,decoder,decoding,metrics,generator}.py; ml/{train,evaluate,data_prep}.py; ml/notebooks/; ml/tests/; backend/app/{main.py,api/v1,services,db,core,schemas.py}; backend/tests/; frontend/ (Vite + React + Tailwind).
RULES: type hints, small functions, a pytest test for every module, no hard-coded paths (use arguments or env vars), no secrets in code, weights and data stay out of git.